    "chromiumOwner": "The held first real player request waited 39031 ms during background-page UI rAF actions, beyond the production 12000 ms request budget. Bringing the acted-on page to the foreground reduces this to a few seconds and preserves all ownership assertions. BFCache was not observed: pagehide.persisted=false and the owning client ID changed. The shared additional-page Puppeteer HTTP transport ensures equal fixture transport but was insufficient alone to fix the failure.",
    "chromiumGc": "The prior owner scenario did not finish; its pending work/stages contaminated the following absolute cache count. With the owner scenario completing, the unchanged product removes only the explicitly seeded orphan and preserves committed/foreign keys.",
    "firefox": "Firefox 153.0 protocol override updates navigator.onLine after an offline reload without delivering a native online event. The standalone no-Pletina control reproduces it with and without QA clock; unreloaded positive controls receive trusted native events. Final FIFO recovery uses a real online document reload and reports automaticOnlineResume=false.",
    "networkRestoreOrdering": "Controlled providers and interception are restored before the browser online event, preventing a QA-only availability race. No synthetic online/offline events are dispatched."
  },
